<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n65939" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέλε</span></b>  (B), 
			Att.
		 voc., used as a familiar address to both sexes, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ μ.</span>
		<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>my friend</i>! <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				671
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Nu.</u>
				33
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				1192
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>V.</u>
				1400
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Pax</u>
				137
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>Ec.</u>
				120
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				133
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νὴ Δία, ὦ μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>Tht.</u>
					178e
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τί κόπτεις, ὦ μ.</span>; <i><span class="en">
				Men.
				457
			</span></i>: sarcastically, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">διαρραγείης, ὦ μ.</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Ar.
					<u>Av.</u>
					1257
				</span></i>
			. (Gramm. expl. it by <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὦ ἐπι-μελ-είας
				ἄξιε καὶ οἷον με-μελ-ημένε</span>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
			</span></i> l.c. (who says it was originally used by women only), or
			connect it with <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">μέλεος</span>, Sch.<i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Eq.</u>
				668
			</span></i>: but it is perh. voc. of <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Μέλος</span> 'good', cf. Lat.
		<i>melior.</i>)</div>
